282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Gastric cancer is a major health concern globally, often detected at advanced stages due to non-specific early symptoms. Early diagnosis is paramount, as it significantly increases the five-year survival rate. Current diagnostic methods rely heavily on endoscopy and subsequent histopathological examination, which are time-consuming and prone to human error or inter-observer variability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (1.2 Project Focus)
/E (1.2 Project Focus)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project focuses on leveraging the power of Deep Learning to automate and enhance the diagnostic process. We utilize a Convolutional Neural Network \(CNN\), which excels at pattern recognition in image data, to analyze endoscopic images and accurately classify them for the presence of gastric abnormalities, including cancer-related findings.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (1.3 Dataset)
/E (1.3 Dataset)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The project is built upon the GastroVision - Gastrointestinal Disease Detection dataset from Kaggle, a large-scale collection of 8,000 clinically annotated GI endoscopy images. The dataset's diversity, featuring 27 different classes of findings, provides a robust foundation for training a highly accurate and generalizable detection model)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
