/E ([1] Title: Deep Learning for Gastric Cancer Detection: A Convolutional Neural Network Approach Author: Wang et al., 2019)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This study proposed a CNN-based system for automated gastric cancer detection using endoscopic images. The model was trained on a large dataset of annotated stomach images and achieved an overall accuracy exceeding 90%. The CNN automatically learned discriminative features such as texture and tissue structure, outperforming traditional image processing and machine learning methods. The research demonstrated that deep learning can significantly reduce diagnostic time and improve consistency compared to manual expert evaluations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
